{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And a man who takes his sister.</b> In a place where they are not aware of it, and afterward the matter becomes known." "The meaning of <b>and he sees her nakedness</b> — either 'sees' as in 'his father and mother he curses' — 'and sees' — as in 'uncovered.'" "The meaning of <b>and she sees his nakedness</b> — that both of them agreed to this." "<b>It is ḥesed.</b> Derived from 'lest the listener show you ḥesed'; its meaning is an addition in sexual immorality." "<b>His sister's nakedness he uncovered.</b> By force." "<b>He shall bear his iniquity.</b> Alone. And the reason to mention these things regarding a sister is because they grew up together and they are children playing, and at every opportunity he may be alone with her. And Scripture did not mention a punishment for a son's daughter or a daughter's daughter, because it relied on the oral Torah. Also possible that it did not mention them because of the diminishment of the father's desire, for he is advanced in years by the time he would have a mature daughter. And therefore Scripture did not mention whether the father or the mother, because they are old."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {5 "Reading חוסר (diminishment); the phrase חוסר תאות האב is unusual and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:27.586814782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}